menu "Impo cloud route"

config IMPO_CHINA_RELAY
    bool "Reach Impo through the mainland China relay when in mainland China"
    default y
    help
        From mainland China, connections to gadgets.impo.ai (Cloudflare) often
        fail or stall. With this on, the gadget asks the relay's /where once per
        Wi-Fi address; when the relay says the gadget's public address is in
        mainland China, the gadget dials the relay instead and names
        IMPO_CHINA_RELAY_TLS_NAME in its TLS and Host header. The relay copies
        the bytes of those TLS connections to Cloudflare without decrypting
        them; the TLS session stays with Cloudflare.
        A gateway host other than gadgets.impo.ai is always used as given.

config IMPO_CHINA_RELAY_HOST
    string "Relay host name"
    depends on IMPO_CHINA_RELAY
    default "gadget.itoy.cn"

config IMPO_CHINA_RELAY_PORT
    int "Relay port"
    depends on IMPO_CHINA_RELAY
    range 1 65535
    default 9443

config IMPO_CHINA_RELAY_TLS_NAME
    string "Name the gadget's TLS and Host header carry through the relay"
    depends on IMPO_CHINA_RELAY
    default "gw.itoy.cn"
    help
        Mainland China providers reset TLS connections that name a domain
        without an ICP filing for the server they reach, gadgets.impo.ai
        among them. So through the relay the gadget names a host under the
        relay's filed domain, which Cloudflare serves as a custom hostname of
        the gateway (gw.itoy.cn CNAME saas.impo.ai). The relay forwards only
        this name, and /where says "CN" only to a gadget that sends it.

endmenu
